 "errors": [{"description": "Converse verification: the middle term is written as (x+y+2C)/2, but f(x)+y = x+C+y, so it should be (x+y+C)/2. The stated justification (RMS–AM–GM for x and y+C) is the correct one, so this is a typographical slip that does not affect the argument.", "quote": "\\ge \\frac{x+y+2C}2"}],
 "notes": "Substitution x=f(y) gives f(f(y))=2f(y)-y; iterates force d=f-id ≥ 0; substituting x=f(t) yields the sharp two-sided bound |d(y)-d(t)| ≤ (y-t)^2/(4 min{t,y}); telescoping over a fine partition forces d constant. All algebra checked; converse correct. Full marks."}
